#
# documented-antipattern: HetColl (Heterogeneous Collective)
#
# OntoUML metamodel model — the HetColl anti-pattern (documented in the OntoUML
# anti-pattern catalogue at https://ontouml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/anti-patterns/):
# a collective whose members are not uniform under the collective's unity criterion.
# The collective stereotype is a mereological endurant outside the endurant-SORTAL +
# relator fragment the five native disciplines range over, so the lowerer records an
# HONEST CAPABILITY GAP (an Unsupported construct) rather than a wrong verdict — the
# native fragment cannot yet express, let alone decide, this documented anti-pattern.

@prefix ontouml: <https://w3id.org/ontouml#> .
@prefix ex:      <https://gmeow.example/ontouml-mini-divergence/heterogeneous-collective/> .

ex:Committee a ontouml:Class ; ontouml:stereotype ontouml:collective .
